<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Horní Blatná–Vlčí jámy circuit — Horní Blatná–Vlčí jámy circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Horní Blatná square, follow yellow markings past the Cínová and Konrád mining displays, continue by the Blatná water ditch and take the marked summit spur. Return on the educational trail past Ledová and Vlčí mine pits and the museum at House 127 to the square. Allow about two hours for 4.1 km; height-gain figures are approximate. Stay on marked public paths: mine-pit and tower interiors are excluded. Check current signs and conditions at gates, especially in snow, ice or wet weather.

Geometry uses the complete current captured OpenStreetMap API XML path (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0). This is a descriptive planning route, not navigation-grade, with no elevation data.

